* BEGIN MODEL NCS2250
*
* MODEL FEATURES INCLUDE PROPAGATION DELAY, OUTPUT
* SWING, OUTPUT CURRENT THROUGH THE SUPPLY RAILS,
* OUTPUT CURRENT LIMIT, COMMON MODE VOLTAGE RANGE,
* CMRR, PSRR, INPUT BIAS CURRENT WITH TEMPERATURE
* AND CMV EFFECTS, INPUT CAPACITANCE, OFFSET,
* OFFSET TEMPERATURE EFFECTS, AND QUIESCENT CURRENT.
* MODEL TOTAL SUPPLY VOLTAGE RANGE IS 1.8 TO 5.5 V.
* MODEL TEMP RANGE IS -40 TO +125 DEG C.
* NOTE THAT MODEL IS FUNCTIONAL OVER THIS RANGE BUT
* NOT ALL PARAMETERS TRACK THOSE OF THE REAL PART.
*
* THIS MODEL ONLY SUPPORTS THE PUSH-PULL VERSION 
* OF THE NCS2250
*
* NOTE - FOR ACCURATE BIAS CURRENTS AT ROOM AND COLD
* SET THE SPICE ANALYSIS OPTIONS AS FOLLOWS :
* RELTOL 0.0001 TO 0.00001 AND GMIN 1E-13 TO 1E-14.
* SET BOTH OF THESE OPTIONS AS SMALL AS WILL ALLOW
* CONVERGANCE ON YOUR SIMULATOR. THIS MAY REQUIRE
* ALSO USING PIVREL OR PIVTOL.
*
* PINOUT ORDER +IN -IN +V -V OUT
* PINOUT ORDER  1   2   3  4  5
